    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\ncursorword\n\n### Description\n\nSometime I want to see some matches which isn't really a word but a combination of multiple words or a sub-word.\r\n\r\nIt would be great if the currently visually selected text is defined as \"Cursorword\" and I get matching highlighting for that. ",
