            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thank you for feature request!\r\n\r\nI don't think that this is an appropriate scope for 'mini.cursorword', as it intentionally operates only on current word in (Neo)Vim sense.\r\n\r\nI solve a similar problem (search for visually selected text) with the mapping I found somewhere:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set('v', 'g/', [[y/\\V<C-R>=escape(@\",'/\\')<CR><CR>]])\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf you want to only get highlighting without moving cursor, add `N` after the last `<CR>`. Note, that this affects current search pattern.",
            "created_at": "2022-12-01T16:30:33Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/168#issuecomment-1334033814",
